<title>NETHERLANDS: DUTCH PTT 1996 SALES REACH DFL 21 BILLION.</title>
<headline>DUTCH PTT 1996 SALES REACH DFL 21 BILLION.</headline>
<dateline>THE HAGUE 1997-01-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch post and telecoms group PTT Nederland NV said on Saturday that its 1996 sales reached 21 billion guilders for the first time in the company's history.  </p>
<p>Quoting chairman Wim Dik, who was addressing the company's management, KPN said in a brief statement that net profits also rose &quot;significantly&quot; in 1996 compared to 1995.</p>
<p>However, it added that growth was accompanied by increasingly higher costs and although it expected sales to rise in 1997 there would also be &quot;continued pressure on the margins&quot;.</p>
<p>No additional financial information was given.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
